.TH MARP-ORDER 1 "" "marp-order" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
marp-order \- visual slide sorter for Marp presentations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B marp-order
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpresentation.md\fR ...] [\fB\-\-\fR \fImarp-cli arguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a grid with the slides of a Marp presentation in the browser, where they can be
rearranged by dragging, edited with a live preview, compared and merged with another
deck, and presented with the speaker notes read aloud. Saving rewrites the Markdown file
in the new order without reformatting the slides that were not edited.
.PP
Each file opens in its own tab. Without files, the ones that were open last time are
opened again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fIn\fR
Local server port (default: chosen by the system).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Do not open the browser automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-thumbs
Do not render thumbnails; show only the slide text.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Do not keep thumbnails on disk between runs.
.TP
\fB\-\-marp\-cmd\fR \fIcmd\fR
The marp-cli command (default: \fBmarp\fR, or \fBnpx @marp-team/marp-cli\fR).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
Anything after \fB\-\-\fR is passed on to marp-cli, for example
\fB\-\-theme\-set theme.css\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MARP_ORDER_MARP_CMD
The marp-cli command, as with \fB\-\-marp\-cmd\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/marp-order/
Recently opened files and the last session.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/marp-order/
Thumbnails kept between runs.
.TP
.I .marp-order-backups/
Next to each deck: copies made before the first write of each run.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/guiok/marp-order
